com/bb_api.h: fix bb_quality_t's declared size to match the real wire size

bb_quality_t is declared as 8 bytes (snr, ldpc_err, ldpc_num, gain_a,
gain_b), and used as an array element by BB_GET_USER_QUALITY
(qualities[BB_DATA_USER_MAX]), BB_GET_PEER_QUALITY
(qualities[BB_SLOT_MAX]), and BB_GET_PAIR_RESULT
(quality[BB_SLOT_MAX], not exercised by ar8030-transport).

Confirmed live on real hardware that the real per-entry record on the
wire is 16 bytes, not 8 -- session_ioctl.c's own io_rpc_cb() reply-
length clamp (patch 0027) was silently truncating both
BB_GET_USER_QUALITY ("reply datalen=160 exceeds expected 80,
truncating") and BB_GET_PEER_QUALITY ("128... 64") on every single
call. Confirmed by rebuilding libar8030_client.so with a temporarily
oversized element type (32 bytes, well past any guess) and dumping the
raw, now-untruncated reply: bytes 0-7 of entry 0 match the 5 documented
fields exactly (cross-validated against ar8030-transport's own
ar8030-linkctl status output before this fix); bytes 8-15 of entry 0
are real, non-zero, currently-undecoded data (not padding); bytes 16+
of entry 0, and the entirety of every other array entry, read back as
zero on this firmware's single-user-mode link. 10*16=160 and 8*16=128
match the observed (truncated) wire sizes for the two calls exactly,
confirming the real per-entry stride is 16 bytes with no slack, not a
larger array length (BB_DATA_USER_MAX/BB_SLOT_MAX are correct
elsewhere -- e.g. BB_GET_STATUS's own arrays of the same nominal
lengths never triggered this warning).

This matters in practice, not just for correctness: ar8030-transport's
tx/bitrate_ctl.c added a fast (~1/s) BB_GET_USER_QUALITY poll to feed
LDPC block-error ratio into its bitrate control loop (radio-repair-
pressure signal, mirroring the vendor's own retx-driven backoff), and
the truncation warning fired on every single call, unconditionally
spamming stderr/the tx log. This patch fixes the actual bug (wrong
struct size) rather than just slowing the poll down to make the
symptom rarer.

The extra 8 bytes are added as `reserved` (not decoded) rather than
guessed at -- same reasoning as 0029's own comment: this only costs a
few bytes on host-side RPC payload structs, not a wire-format change,
and getting the SIZE right (so the daemon's real reply is never
truncated) doesn't require knowing what every byte means yet.

diff --git a/com/bb_api.h b/com/bb_api.h
index 3b0c9a1..1a2b3c4 100644
--- a/com/bb_api.h
+++ b/com/bb_api.h
@@ -400,12 +400,35 @@
 typedef uint16_t chan_t;                                        /**<@note 统一信道=子信道(高Byte)+主信道(低Byte)*/

 /**定义8030物理用户信号质量结构体*/
+/* Fixed on real hardware (2026-09): this struct's declared 8-byte size does
+ * not match its real per-entry size on the wire wherever it is used as an
+ * array (BB_GET_USER_QUALITY's qualities[BB_DATA_USER_MAX],
+ * BB_GET_PEER_QUALITY's qualities[BB_SLOT_MAX], and by extension
+ * BB_GET_PAIR_RESULT's quality[BB_SLOT_MAX], though that one is not
+ * exercised by ar8030-transport). Confirmed by capturing the FULL,
+ * untruncated reply with a temporarily oversized element type: the real
+ * per-entry record is 16 bytes -- the 5 documented fields below plus 8
+ * more genuinely-populated-but-currently-undecoded trailing bytes, not
+ * padding (bytes past 16 for the same entry, and the entirety of every
+ * other array entry actually unpopulated in this firmware's single-user
+ * mode, read back as zero). 10*16=160 and 8*16=128 match the observed
+ * wire sizes for the two calls exactly -- this is how the bug was first
+ * noticed, via session_ioctl.c's own io_rpc_cb() "reply datalen=160
+ * exceeds expected 80, truncating" / "128... 64" warnings (ar8030-
+ * transport's tx/bitrate_ctl.c calls BB_GET_USER_QUALITY on a fast poll
+ * path, so this fired continuously). Adding `reserved` below (not decoded
+ * yet) fixes the size so the daemon's real reply is never truncated
+ * again -- mirrors bb_config.h's own BB_CONFIG_MAX_CHAN_NUM 32->60 fix in
+ * spirit (correct a host-side struct size against what the real hardware
+ * actually sends), except this one is measured exactly rather than padded
+ * with headroom, since the real size is now confirmed, not estimated. */
 typedef struct {
     uint16_t snr;                                               /**<@note 物理用户接收信噪比，转化db公式：10log(snr/36)*/
     uint16_t ldpc_err;                                          /**<@note 交织块中解码错误的LDPC块个数*/
     uint16_t ldpc_num;                                          /**<@note 交织块中总的LDPC块个数*/
     uint8_t  gain_a;                                            /**<@note A路天线接收信号强度*/
     uint8_t  gain_b;                                            /**<@note B路天线接收信号强度*/
+    uint8_t  reserved[8];                                       /**<@note Confirmed real/populated on the wire (not padding) but not yet decoded -- see this struct's own comment above*/
 } bb_quality_t;

 /**定义8030支持的的频段类型*/
